WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.170
What if you could speed up an old
computer without deleting a single file?

2
00:00:05.220 --> 00:00:08.890
Inside is a magnetic hard
disk: a spinning platter,

3
00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:11.570
and a read write head on a moving arm.

4
00:00:11.620 --> 00:00:13.510
A utility program runs.

5
00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.950
It deletes nothing.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.710
It only moves data around the disk.

7
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.850
Afterwards, the same files open faster.

8
00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:24.130
So why would just moving data around help?

9
00:00:24.180 --> 00:00:27.070
In this mission, you'll
meet utility software:

10
00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:31.330
system software that does housekeeping
jobs the operating system may not do well

11
00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:32.270
enough.

12
00:00:32.320 --> 00:00:35.530
You'll see how a hard disk
stores files in blocks.

13
00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:38.950
And why the head has to travel
to each block to read it.

14
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.510
Your mission: explain why shuffling
files around could make an old hard drive

15
00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.240
faster.
